// The fuzzer's trace normalization renumbers `#<digits>` (and
// `#<lowercase><digits>`, `'_<digits>`) inside every string a program
// produces, so two engines that differ only there compare equal.
//
// Command:
//   timeout -s KILL 180 /home/eric/tmp/review-2026-11-16/bin/graphix-fuzz run \
//     design/review-2026-11-16/repro/x-traits-abstract-fuzz-trace-renumbers-program-strings.gx
//
// Expected: the trace the oracle compares holds the four values the program
// produced, as the shell prints them:
//   "item #0 of 0"  "item #1 of 1"  "item #2 of 2"  "item #3 of 3"
//
// Observed (every mode):
//   Interp/InLanguage: Trace([0:"item #0 of 0" 1:"item #0 of 1" 2:"item #0 of 2" 3:"item #0 of 3"])
//
// A `Display` impl printing "#ff0000" for a colour (design/traits.md's own
// example) is renumbered the same way: "#ff0000" and "#ff0001" are both
// "#ff0".
let n = 0;
n <- select n { k if k < 3 => k + 1, _ => never() };
"item #[n] of [n]"
